                        "glosses": [
                            "Gradually, little by little (an inch at a time)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "idiomatic",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e76a67bf-5d34-4c1d-a1d4-9e83bd666dcb",
                                "sense_id": "1a484afe-c8e0-349a-ae96-8404daf22227",
                                "text": "Those who are not thus slippery in the tail, are light of finger; and of these the most pernicious are those who beggar you inchmeal."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0c92483-ad10-483a-80c1-7fd48cae494a",
                                "sense_id": "1a484afe-c8e0-349a-ae96-8404daf22227",
                                "text": "I am a sanguinary murderer of time, and would kill him inchmeal just now."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bca08a05-322f-49c8-b6fd-7a81aa0e4c5f",
                                "sense_id": "1a484afe-c8e0-349a-ae96-8404daf22227",
                                "text": "All the infections that the sun sucks up / From bogs, fens, flats, on Prosper fall, and make him / By inch-meal a disease!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "939839c1-7a5d-4058-8350-e72f47795c47",
                                "sense_id": "1a484afe-c8e0-349a-ae96-8404daf22227",
                                "text": "He could be as patient as Death, that inchmeal stalker of his prey; he could be as ruthless as the sea, and incredibly generous upon occasion."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
